{"base_rate":0.5049019607843137,"brier":0.27562173202614376,"bss":-0.102592905892531,"bss_hi":0.03374384890175237,"bss_lo":-0.2666501139217049,"chart":{"base":[716.7,84.3],"fp":[128.1,229.5],"lead":"62,278.8 272,265.1 482,263.3 692,240.9","note":{"base":"skill -0.10 — higher than 8% of cities","fp":"low end -7pp, high end +32pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.8 °C — better than 91% of cities","rel":"promised 28% → rained 7%; promised 99% → rained 71%"},"rel":"241,437.7 553.1,325.6 683.8,160.1"},"country":"HN","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.30132352941176466,"ess":304.5415241215652,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for La Ceiba</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The La Ceiba rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>77%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(9%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 612 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 3.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.10, ranked 197 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(183&ndash;201) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>47%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>70%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>59</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>85%</td><td class='num'><b>41%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>94%</td><td class='num'><b>42%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>77%</b></td><td class='num'>306</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>La Ceiba</b> <span class=\"muted\">Honduras</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>-0.10</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>183&ndash;201\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>612 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    La Ceiba &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for La Ceiba\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"91.48491803278688,322.327868852459 225.7147540983607,167.18032786885246 306.52,85.86440677966101 360.4668852459016,41.86885245901635 391.36843749999997,23.6875 410.7621568627451,18.0 410.7621568627451,21.59836601307188 391.36843749999997,63.5 360.4668852459016,107.50819672131149 306.52,172.23728813559322 225.7147540983607,256.6885245901639 91.48491803278688,370.0655737704918\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"198.2156862745098\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"198.2156862745098\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"91.48491803278688,376.0327868852459 225.7147540983607,340.2295081967213 306.52,295.62711864406776 360.4668852459016,232.81967213114754 391.36843749999997,228.4375 410.7621568627451,102.45751633986924\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 61 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"91.48491803278688\" cy=\"376.0327868852459\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 47%&amp;#10;It rained 11% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 61 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"225.7147540983607\" cy=\"340.2295081967213\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 70%&amp;#10;It rained 24% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 59 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"306.52\" cy=\"295.62711864406776\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 85%&amp;#10;It rained 41% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 61 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"360.4668852459016\" cy=\"232.81967213114754\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 94%&amp;#10;It rained 42% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"391.36843749999997\" cy=\"228.4375\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 77% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 306 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.7621568627451\" cy=\"102.45751633986924\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(50%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In La Ceiba the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.19) and least in\n<b>spring</b> (-1.25).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>147</td><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'>-1.247</td><td class='num'>44.7%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>162</td><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'>-0.375</td><td class='num'>35.8%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>151</td><td class='num'>69%</td><td class='num'>0.041</td><td class='num'>20.0%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>152</td><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'>0.189</td><td class='num'>20.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":15.76667,"lon":-86.83333,"n":612,"n_cities":213,"name":"La Ceiba","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.29,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.09459016393442622,"n":61,"obs":0.01639344262295082,"sig":true},{"hi":0.63,"lo":0.29,"mean":0.47377049180327874,"n":61,"obs":0.11475409836065574,"sig":tr